#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36c72f44-8cad-59b9-b978-9486a3fb8e1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{51\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538159} {:answer/id #uuid "5035e854-d3a5-5790-9eb6-eb2c68c9a904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538167} {:answer/id #uuid "617c9ac0-970c-54d5-982f-e31ce5878129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{57\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538172} {:answer/id #uuid "6fdec5d1-edeb-5afe-bba5-e721dfcadba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538176} {:answer/id #uuid "a844d8b0-bab6-5d45-822f-ff3c2b83d953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a844d8b0-bab6-5d45-822f-ff3c2b83d953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538191} :answer-field/id #uuid "8546cdef-82e7-5512-88cc-d73209e88c5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0093dc0f-6d13-5136-8a41-4ec719538cf8" :question/problem "![](images/57/573013be1dc56a1ae4d0765b81b8e94006b8402a6da9706b118d43e286fb8291.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}6y\\,dx+9x\\,dy,\n$$ where $D$ is the region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=6y$ and $Q(x,y)=9x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=6,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}6y\\,dx+9x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(9-6)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3\\,\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\frac{\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{17\\pi}{2}  \\\\  & =\\frac{51\\pi}{2} .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d51d6ac-4c27-54cd-b01f-880b60999800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "492\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538165} {:answer/id #uuid "55780946-8d44-5da2-bf53-437f89466c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538169} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba0634d-fd89-51ca-bf2d-52c72119346e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538185} {:answer/id #uuid "a36d97e0-3b01-5109-9dd3-61dfaf2cc216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538189} {:answer/id #uuid "b5bd23ab-0096-5f66-92c3-71109a692c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-108\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55780946-8d44-5da2-bf53-437f89466c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538169} :answer-field/id #uuid "1574ac62-0771-511a-8354-4c35bed7f7ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28489039-fdfa-503c-aed0-769a751abddb" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1e97d150acbe82bf31d0a0e371122ae567d62279b66a5db2a3164180248a5e71.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}-13dx+12x\\,dy,\n$$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-13$ and $Q(x,y)=12x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}-13dx+12x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(12-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {5}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {4}^{2}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (25\\pi -16\\pi ) \\\\  & =108\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338fccf2-f549-585f-af57-a920eb07c34e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-560" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538158} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0eacde-8684-5144-862a-ff9207abd200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-704" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538166} {:answer/id #uuid "ae9d1961-35d2-57dc-9b39-45b4e2119f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-624" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538194} {:answer/id #uuid "b541b542-9c57-5006-bc4a-4c3a995d3adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "560" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538196} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f897dc-a433-57f6-aaa4-ca8f6e3515d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-976" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "338fccf2-f549-585f-af57-a920eb07c34e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-560" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538158} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9b981ed-6379-5393-ba8b-72c70879308f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3c303577-d49b-5f6d-ae6a-7c78499f5f3d" :question/problem "![](images/24/245fb5eea54d303236a038f3d1b8253bc6c2e70426bcf0e5f48a40704b47d669.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}9y\\,dx+5x\\,dy,\n$$ where $D$ is the region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=9y$ and $Q(x,y)=5x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=9,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}9y\\,dx+5x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-9)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-4\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-4{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (16\\cdot 12-{4}^{2}-{6}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (192-16-36) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 140 \\\\  & =-560.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538171 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a326d88-270c-56a5-934b-0ecf38037461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2016" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538155} {:answer/id #uuid "8ead2f2d-0fbf-581f-a47f-ce631f9f623c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2520" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538182} {:answer/id #uuid "bb86ad3f-4859-534b-a0ba-424359b6630f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2184" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538199} {:answer/id #uuid "c22625c0-8ffa-57ca-b447-c4331e833add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1960" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538201} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b5dba7-939f-52a8-bc6c-dd82a8901707" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1960" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c22625c0-8ffa-57ca-b447-c4331e833add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1960" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538201} :answer-field/id #uuid "aca3e355-2de5-5a67-a052-93dfcc4e2cf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5c5f644e-f3a9-5505-9151-ceb09a68b40b" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d1b2d83da42a1a95525ce3359e947800af884cd29f1ead6d9dbe4cee1c8dfb40.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}8y\\,dx-6x\\,dy,\n$$ where $D$ is the region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=8y$ and $Q(x,y)=-6x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=8,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}8y\\,dx-6x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6-8)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-14\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-14{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-14\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =-14\\cdot (16\\cdot 10-{4}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =-14\\cdot (160-16-4) \\\\  & =-14\\cdot 140 \\\\  & =-1960.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f16cfc2-f619-5e86-9b3b-77f85371764c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-240\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538175} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d7754c-2a5d-5712-9b09-74a2ab844f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538198} {:answer/id #uuid "d9350129-4bd1-5631-8b78-17fb3a4316d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "250\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538205} {:answer/id #uuid "e2985cfb-93fe-5a5d-a26a-0e73d7c15c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "245\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538208} {:answer/id #uuid "f2669bc2-2483-5613-be28-070c44b1ac89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2669bc2-2483-5613-be28-070c44b1ac89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538213} :answer-field/id #uuid "58154caa-247c-59c1-b74c-77e6b506e7df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "874f8d64-a3fc-5a12-89b8-9d65bb0715ce" :question/problem "![](images/48/483ce10aae9978fbc4c1b5a71173ab10b52bca0b15c84f01d7adb7247e82e436.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}-2y\\,dx+3x\\,dy,\n$$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-2y$ and $Q(x,y)=3x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}-2y\\,dx+3x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3-(-2))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}5\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {7}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 48\\pi  \\\\  & =240\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45b042c5-5ebd-5d31-a6cc-baf65a7e1e9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1288" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538163} {:answer/id #uuid "7f99a411-d07d-5e1d-8fc7-8e4bebe92bec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1288" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538178} {:answer/id #uuid "a27bcbcc-285b-5d7f-9591-69f818793844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1512" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538187} {:answer/id #uuid "a4d2bb25-05b6-5674-817e-51dd14f03467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1848" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538190} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b8573b-d9b9-5a64-bb38-a1d9124d5ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1344" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f99a411-d07d-5e1d-8fc7-8e4bebe92bec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1288" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538178} :answer-field/id #uuid "c84981b5-b8c1-55f7-8be1-ae3f5a997562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538203}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9687dcec-a46d-5800-a061-342d9450fae3" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4a1b8a23b4fb0d081f9d88748735e02b3a173843e5c4a1a40e70e6ba4e7335ad.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}-6y\\,dx+8x\\,dy,\n$$ where $D$ is the region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-6y$ and $Q(x,y)=8x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-6,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}-6y\\,dx+8x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(8-(-6))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}14\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =14{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =14\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =14\\cdot (14\\cdot 8-{4}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =14\\cdot (112-16-4) \\\\  & =14\\cdot 92 \\\\  & =1288.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538192 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "047f2b36-8964-5e1c-ba40-c92c874a8db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2350\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538152} {:answer/id #uuid "433dda26-4bb9-5114-b487-b99e5b406903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1925\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538162} {:answer/id #uuid "461804c5-46bb-5d96-af8e-d970cc58a5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1800\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538164} {:answer/id #uuid "550a93f5-da6d-5738-b24c-952715ec8a29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1700\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538168} {:answer/id #uuid "da4d1cc7-9202-56d5-99b4-8e92451ba91c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1700\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "550a93f5-da6d-5738-b24c-952715ec8a29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1700\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538168} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3960239-93b4-5860-9265-ba5ce587e842" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa14acb3-297f-5aab-a401-2c7b97eae563" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d2039c49121a2da30efa96b7d456a043aa3860bc19399e67385c3f3268f6c0f8.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}-13y\\,dx+12x\\,dy,\n$$ where $D$ is the region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-13y$ and $Q(x,y)=12x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-13,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}-13y\\,dx+12x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(12-(-13))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}25\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =25{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =25\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {9}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =25\\cdot (81\\pi-9\\pi-4\\pi) \\\\  & =25\\cdot 68\\pi \\\\  & =1700\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538200 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a0efce4-e40a-5e17-b861-06b7b2120749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "216\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538160} {:answer/id #uuid "66452399-e90b-503f-8285-f8443359f389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "510\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538173} {:answer/id #uuid "70f313eb-7bf3-576e-aabf-93fe0ff7e116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538177} {:answer/id #uuid "a2a4a1df-b5f1-5dd4-9b8a-e7cd9b8d7028" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-78\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538188} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf58509-b20b-5513-9bd9-8e1fec479d3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "294\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70f313eb-7bf3-576e-aabf-93fe0ff7e116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538177} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b9efb0e-1e55-59e1-a247-642db1fe26b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf10ccdd-2f45-595c-a4ea-08a81d57feab" :question/problem "![](images/83/83357e8db109cd09ddcc51043caff588225edfd1b8f7b98dbb640a230ea7843d.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}-13dx+6x\\,dy,\n$$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-13$ and $Q(x,y)=6x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}-13dx+6x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(6-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}6\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {7}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {6}^{2}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (49\\pi -36\\pi ) \\\\  & =78\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12575b41-8b98-5c1d-826e-16aacaf6e698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "760\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538153} {:answer/id #uuid "32f53203-099b-5874-889b-f83efd77d8a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-684\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538157} {:answer/id #uuid "861fadab-9825-5be8-8460-de34cdfe93f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "684\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538180} {:answer/id #uuid "92135252-c7a2-5a2e-b8bb-edf11e6375d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "855\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538183} {:answer/id #uuid "ef813cc5-c174-5a71-87e1-585aabb2bfa