e {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<\\frac{5}{2},\\,y\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540338} {:answer/id #uuid "586c6aa5-223a-5a5c-96e3-2148d836634c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{5}{2},\\,y>4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540346} {:answer/id #uuid "74da7215-0e5c-5995-98e1-afdd34f0ecd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{5}{2},\\,y>4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540356} {:answer/id #uuid "8809df57-8c37-5023-bc33-262b767089d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{5}{2},\\,y<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540363} {:answer/id #uuid "abe91d82-658b-5b20-ac12-53f7c0a01f9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{2},\\,y=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "586c6aa5-223a-5a5c-96e3-2148d836634c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{5}{2},\\,y>4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540346} :answer-field/id #uuid "068b709a-b75b-59ef-9da3-f65183f42816" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "50b6c465-a48b-5670-bf04-569c56432b66" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=- 2 t^{2} + 6 t - 2,\\,y=t^{2} + 2 t + 1,\\,t>1,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ complete the square:\n\n$$\nx=- 2 t^{2} + 6 t - 2=\\frac{5}{2} - 2 \\left(t - \\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{2} .\n$$\n\nThe vertex parameter is $t=\\frac{3}{2}$, which is admissible. The vertex value is $\\frac{5}{2}$ and is attained. The coordinate is unbounded below. Consequently, $x\\le \\frac{5}{2}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ complete the square:\n\n$$\ny=t^{2} + 2 t + 1=\\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} .\n$$\n\nThe vertex parameter is $t=-1$, which is outside the given domain. On the given half-line the endpoint value is $4$, and the endpoint is excluded. The coordinate is unbounded above. Consequently, $y>4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f5cb103-e2a6-55dd-88b4-ff951035454a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,\\,y=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540323} {:answer/id #uuid "241da18c-4f54-5fdb-83a6-d4aebd28f761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 4,\\,y\\ge -9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540331} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3a878f-e656-5812-b166-5fe192c2113d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 4,\\,y\\ge -9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540340} {:answer/id #uuid "6624af64-32b4-5f0d-9f8f-7024a71f8688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 4,\\,y\\le -9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540349} {:answer/id #uuid "edb1276f-e5da-5e57-8127-c419090d77fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>4,\\,y>-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a3a878f-e656-5812-b166-5fe192c2113d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 4,\\,y\\ge -9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540340} :answer-field/id #uuid "657d489d-712a-511d-98b9-58b6832dfb26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8ae8b975-365c-5028-a76a-4fbbd7e53014" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2 t^{2} + 2 t,\\,y=t^{2} + 4 t - 5,\\,t\\le -2,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ complete the square:\n\n$$\nx=2 t^{2} + 2 t=2 \\left(t + \\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2} - \\frac{1}{2} .\n$$\n\nThe vertex parameter is $t=- \\frac{1}{2}$, which is outside the given domain. On the given half-line the endpoint value is $4$, and the endpoint is included. The coordinate is unbounded above. Consequently, $x\\ge 4.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ complete the square:\n\n$$\ny=t^{2} + 4 t - 5=\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2} - 9 .\n$$\n\nThe vertex parameter is $t=-2$, which is admissible. The vertex value is $-9$ and is attained. The coordinate is unbounded above. Consequently, $y\\ge -9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c4932ea-c763-57bf-bad2-c7101a0f7441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-17,\\,y>5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540336} {:answer/id #uuid "7958ee9e-9348-53fd-b695-010ab2d6a521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -17,\\,y\\ge 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540358} {:answer/id #uuid "93cee4f9-9562-5921-8231-68748001f777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -17,\\,y\\ge 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540365} {:answer/id #uuid "e391ff1c-3b92-599a-89bb-61eb55e3d44a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -17,\\,y\\le 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540382} {:answer/id #uuid "fa3e0eb1-ba4e-56b2-8b3f-ee6c8a0f6f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-17,\\,y=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93cee4f9-9562-5921-8231-68748001f777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -17,\\,y\\ge 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540365} :answer-field/id #uuid "17948856-41f0-5963-a4f3-c7e1dade903e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "94f58f96-598e-54a4-8607-cf21c3064688" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=- t^{2} - 2 t - 2,\\,y=t^{2} - 2 t + 2,\\,t\\ge 3,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ complete the square:\n\n$$\nx=- t^{2} - 2 t - 2=- \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} - 1 .\n$$\n\nThe vertex parameter is $t=-1$, which is outside the given domain. On the given half-line the endpoint value is $-17$, and the endpoint is included. The coordinate is unbounded below. Consequently, $x\\le -17.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ complete the square:\n\n$$\ny=t^{2} - 2 t + 2=\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2} + 1 .\n$$\n\nThe vertex parameter is $t=1$, which is outside the given domain. On the given half-line the endpoint value is $5$, and the endpoint is included. The coordinate is unbounded above. Consequently, $y\\ge 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540388 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e45272e-8afe-5b6f-978b-ccf4afd87d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540327} {:answer/id #uuid "20878ee0-343d-5e0d-8708-37cd87317f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in\\mathbb{R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540330} {:answer/id #uuid "2adcd39f-66b4-5d95-89d7-09316483002a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540332} {:answer/id #uuid "b83ed8c1-dba8-5153-9161-a609f46b224c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540373} {:answer/id #uuid "d83b4653-9428-53c9-a5f0-e0c582fa15fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e45272e-8afe-5b6f-978b-ccf4afd87d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540327} :answer-field/id #uuid "6864f1bb-68b1-5d61-8dc5-9e6625f3eed5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb3e9e45-5ced-52f5-ba77-5853c61cad57" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=- 2 t - 2,\\,y=t,\\,t>2,\n$$\n\ndetermine the range of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ evaluate the endpoint: $x(2)=-6$. The coefficient of $t$ is $-2$, so the coordinate is monotone on the given half-line. The parameter endpoint is excluded. The range is $x<-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540454 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "176720a9-acff-5477-a486-6f30c8128839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-68i+41j-32k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540445} {:answer/id #uuid "22951b7e-d04f-5c4d-9f1f-3713d00b281e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28i-31j+16k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540449} {:answer/id #uuid "62947b76-220e-5406-98bf-d0a9d0e48979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31i-16j-28k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540464} {:answer/id #uuid "af6aac4d-efa7-5258-9ee3-df10cdfaf02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28i-31j-16k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540487} {:answer/id #uuid "c196d5c3-3941-50ec-b6c4-8cb946447b72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28i+31j-16k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c196d5c3-3941-50ec-b6c4-8cb946447b72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28i+31j-16k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540492} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b5cb85c-1fb0-58d6-b021-acc3af2b4754" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e010a3d-bc78-5472-b0fd-3b9999a59e7f" :question/problem "Let $u=6i+8j+5k$ and $v=-i-4j-6k.$ Find $u\\times v.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 6 & 8 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ -4 & -6\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -6\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =((8)(-6)-(5)(-4))i-((6)(-6)-(5)(-1))j+((6)(-4)-(8)(-1))k \\\\  & =(-48-(-20))i-(-36-(-5))j+(-24-(-8))k \\\\  & =-28i+31j-16k \\\\  & =⟨-28,31,-16⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540456 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c322d1d5-fa93-5b4d-95c0-830b54df1e15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c322d1d5-fa93-5b4d-95c0-830b54df1e15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540494} :answer-field/id #uuid "672d067c-a7f8-5d32-b7dd-2a9c164ead57" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540466} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "837c5d7e-5c7a-55c0-a1dd-2c6a1f5a7c94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "837c5d7e-5c7a-55c0-a1dd-2c6a1f5a7c94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540472} :answer-field/id #uuid "71bcb1f3-c0ec-5af1-9ecb-8c82c317c35c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540468} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "674927f3-92ff-5d26-a00d-cb0a1f3ad243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{19}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "674927f3-92ff-5d26-a00d-cb0a1f3ad243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{19}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540467} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fdcf7e5-dd52-509d-8532-451e7e4957a8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3c34ce35-aef6-5c54-826e-13e18dd80841" :question/problem "Let $u=⟨3,\\frac{7}{2},-2⟩$ and $v=⟨\\frac{1}{2},-1,5⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$\n\n$u\\times v=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & \\frac{7}{2} & -2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -1 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{7}{2} & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}3 & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)(5)-(-2)(-1))i-((3)(5)-(-2)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right))j+((3)(-1)-\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right))k \\\\  & =(\\frac{35}{2}-(2))i-(15-(-1))j+(-3-\\left(\\frac{7}{4}\\right))k \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{2}i-16j-\\frac{19}{4}k \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{31}{2},-16,-\\frac{19}{4}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540471 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "083370b1-ba72-5090-86d4-3a98f815ca42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-\\frac{79}{10},\\frac{17}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540442} {:answer/id #uuid "3aa1026d-b21a-538c-9efb-fc6dfba4a3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{79}{10},-\\frac{17}{5},2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540455} {:answer/id #uuid "83d427ec-a05b-57c1-b3a1-26cb9989f5f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,-\\frac{121}{10},\\frac{23}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540473} {:answer/id #uuid "ad06b859-0b73-5512-aaa2-eb46767b7e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\frac{79}{10},-\\frac{17}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540486} {:answer/id #uuid "c03d7484-43b2-53d9-a04d-756366cee69e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-\\frac{79}{10},-\\frac{17}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad06b859-0b73-5512-aaa2-eb46767b7e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\frac{79}{10},-\\frac{17}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540486} :answer-field/id #uuid "43a5d5e9-93a6-5b25-801f-3e73c6bcbbe5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8258bec8-eb13-513a-bb18-127d6cd09d35" :question/problem "Let $u=⟨\\frac{3}{5},2,5⟩$ and $v=⟨2,1,\\frac{7}{2}⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & 2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & \\frac{7}{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{7}{2}\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & 5 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{7}{2}\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =((2)\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)-(5)(1))i-(\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)-(5)(2))j+(\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)(1)-(2)(2))k \\\\  & =(7-(5))i-(\\frac{21}{10}-(10))j+(\\frac{3}{5}-(4))k \\\\  & =2i+\\frac{79}{10}j-\\frac{17}{5}k \\\\  & =⟨2,\\frac{79}{10},-\\frac{17}{5}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d28dfd8-9152-532d-98b5-be529cedeb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d28dfd8-9152-532d-98b5-be529cedeb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540448} :answer-field/id #uuid "49194f54-48df-5f32-8a0a-7f4e3cec0b72" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540460} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85c62749-6648-5016-91ac-a762bf5d